      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>Our mission is to bridge the gap between undergraduate studies and physician associate/assistant (PA) school while providing the convenience of a centralized platform where pre-PAs can form a community amongst themselves and experienced professionals. In addition to forming an inclusive and diverse pre-PA community, we aim to offer affordable resources and beneficial opportunities to help enhance the CASPA application process and increase our members' chances of getting into PA school. Current opportunities include: community service events, campus tours, preparation workshops, mentorship programs, and more. Anyone ranging from current students to graduates can join to learn about the profession. We currently reside in Southern California but hope to expand outward as our organization grows.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>As of current filing, we have gained attraction for over 1052 members with 182 members attending various events including mock interviews, workshops, informational sessions, and social events during the 02/24/2025 - 08/30/2025 period.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>0</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>In total for the current fiscal year, we have accumulated over 29 attendees for our affordable CPR classes, aimed to provide a low-cost stepping stone in obtaining a healthcare career. Ultimately, our CPR classes are aimed towards low-income students who are wishes to pursue an entry-level position in the healthcare field to gain patient care experience for their CASPA application. In total, we have received $1129 from teaching these classes to use for our organization services.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>1129</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>0</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>To celebrate the efforts of our board officers serving during the fiscal year of 2023-2024, we had a board social dinner to discuss accomplishments, met goals, and statistical numbers of audiences reached. The remaining dinner cost was split amongst the co-founders after using $300 funds.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
